"""Wisconsin Heights: the battle of 21 July 1832.  A sample game for
the Grognard engine.

The Black Hawk War.  Black Hawk's band of Sauk and Meskwaki, perhaps a
thousand people, most of them women, children and old people, hungry
and worn out by weeks of flight, has reached the Wisconsin River with
the militia close behind.  While the families build rafts and cross,
Black Hawk and a few dozen warriors must hold off six or seven hundred
mounted volunteers on the heights above the river.  Play either side
against the computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./heights (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.heights.json.  ./heights --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

